[0.000, "o", "ter\u001b[m-to-send against active macOS IME composition\r\n  (\u001b[94m_isImeComposing\u001b[m) and supports \u001b[94mShift + Enter\u001b[m for newlines.\r\n  • \u001b[1mTestability\u001b[m: \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8d42f9d233df8106;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L9-L18\u0007AntigravityAgentSession\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk9b61df54696dced7;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L63-L67\u0007AntigravitySessionBuilder\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 allow \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkdd1b18e687025cbd;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/test/widget_test.dart\u0007widget_test.dart\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 to test streaming,\r\n  error formatting, and session teardown deterministically without spawning real \u001b[94mlocalharness\u001b[m processes.\r\n\n  \u001b[1m#### Potential Issues & Observations\u001b[m\r\n\n  1. \u001b[1mImplicit \u001b[94;22mDirectory.current\u001b[39;1m Workspace in Release \u001b[94;22m.app\u001b[39;1m Builds\u001b[m\n\u001b[58D• Because \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk3eeefdad9f8dac94;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L113-L1"]
[0.000, "o", "38\u0007ChatRepository.buildAgentConfig\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 leaves \u001b[94mworkspaces\u001b[m as \u001b[94mnull\u001b[m by default, launching the release \u001b[94m.app\u001b[m from\r\n\u001b[6CFinder will configure \u001b[94mlocalharness\u001b[m with \u001b[94m/\u001b[m as its workspace root. Built-in file/search tools (\u001b[94mfind\u001b[m, \u001b[94mgrep_search\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[94mlist_dir\u001b[m, \u001b[94mview_file\u001b[m, \u001b[94mwrite_to_file\u001b[m, \u001b[94mfile_edit\u001b[m) remain enabled by default in \u001b[94mCapabilitiesConfig()\u001b[m, meaning the\r\n\u001b[6Cagent's workspace root becomes \u001b[94m/\u001b[m when launched outside a terminal.\n\u001b[66D• \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Explicitly pass an intended workspace directory (such as a dedicated app support/workspace\r\n\u001b[6Cfolder or user-selected directory) or, if this app is intended as a pure chat assistant without filesystem\r\n\u001b[6Caccess, disable built-in file tools via \u001b[94mCapabilitiesConfig(enabledTools: const [])\u001b[m.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mThread Title Locked In at Session Creation\u001b[m\n\u001b[41D• In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd4590c603d32f32f;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_rep"]
[0.000, "o", "ository.dart#L142-L157\u0007ChatRepository.getOrCreateSession\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mbuildAgentConfig\u001b[m embeds \u001b[94mthreadTitle\u001b[m into \u001b[94mCustomSystemInstructions\u001b[m only\r\n\u001b[6Cwhen the session is first created (\u001b[94m_sessions.putIfAbsent\u001b[m). That works well with the current auto-titling flow\r\n\u001b[6C(since auto-titling runs before the first message creates the session), but if thread renaming is ever added\r\n\u001b[6Clater, the existing session's system instructions will retain the initial title.\r\n  3. \u001b[1mComposer State Shared Across Thread Switches\u001b[m\n\u001b[43D• \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jke574019f330a822e;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/markdown_composer.dart#L27-L30\u0007MarkdownComposer\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 holds a single \u001b[94mTextEditingController\u001b[m not keyed by \u001b[94mactiveThreadId\u001b[m. If a user types a draft in\r\n\u001b[6CThread A and clicks Thread B in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8015991529845862;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/thread_sidebar.dart\u0007ThreadSidebar\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, the unsent "]
[0.000, "o", "draft remains in the input box for Thread B.\r\n\n\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m 1. Add a concept of projects that set a working directory for the Antigravity harness.\r\n  2. I'm guessing workspaceOnly enables commands that are inside the sandbox. We should add UI that allows programs to\r\n  be run that want to escape the sandbox, but only after review by the user.\r\n  3. Update README.md and add `/skills/` to `.gitignore`.\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
