[0.000, "o", "───────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[37;1mRequesting permission for:\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m   ls -la ~/.antigravity/bin/ && strings ~/.antigravity/bin/localharness* 2>/dev/null | grep -iE\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[37m\"disable_sandbox|enable_sandbox|sandbox_escape|workspace_containment|policy_decision_request\" | head -n 50\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[1mRun this command?\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[94m> 1. Yes, run command\u001b[K\u001b[m\r\n  2. Yes, and always allow in this conversation for commands that start with 'strings'\r\n  3. Yes, and always allow for commands that start with 'strings' (Persist to settings.json)\u001b[K\r\n  4. No, cancel\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[94;1m↑/↓\u001b[90;22m Navigate · \u001b[94;1mtab\u001b[90;22m Amend · \u001b[94;1mctrl+g\u001b[90;22m edit/expand command\u001b[m\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[90mesc to cancel\u001b[m\u001b[84X\u001b[84C\u001b[2mGemini 4 Argon · medium\r\u001b[m\u001b[?2026l"]
[3.522, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\u001b[J\u001b[31A\t\u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Explicitly pass an intended workspace directory (such as a dedicated app support/workspace\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[6Cfolder or user-selected directory) or, if this app is intended as a pure chat assistant without filesystem\r\n\u001b[6Caccess, disable built-in file tools via \u001b[94mCapabilitiesConfig(enabledTools: const [])\u001b[m.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mThread Title Locked In at Session Creation\u001b[m\n\u001b[42D\u001b[1K • In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd4590c603d32f32f;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L142-L157\u0007ChatRepository.getOrCreateSession\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mbuildAgentConfig\u001b[m embeds \u001b[94mthreadTitle\u001b[m into \u001b[94mCustomSystemInstructions\u001b[m only\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K when the session is first created (\u001b[94m_sessions.putIfAbsent\u001b[m). That works well with the current auto-titling flow\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K (since auto-titling runs before the first message creates the session), but if thread renaming is ever added\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K later, the existing session's system instructions will retain the initial title"]
