[3.598, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[0 q\r\u001b[J\u001b[31A\u001b[5C\u001b[1K • \u001b[1mRecommendation\u001b[m: Explicitly pass an intended workspace directory (such as a dedicated app support/workspace\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K folder or user-selected directory) or, if this app is intended as a pure chat assistant without filesystem\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K access, disable built-in file tools via \u001b[94mCapabilitiesConfig(enabledTools: const [])\u001b[m.\r\n  2. \u001b[1mThread Title Locked In at Session Creation\u001b[m\u001b[K\n\u001b[41D• In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd4590c603d32f32f;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L142-L157\u0007ChatRepository.getOrCreateSession\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mbuildAgentConfig\u001b[m embeds \u001b[94mthreadTitle\u001b[m into \u001b[94mCustomSystemInstructions\u001b[m only\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K when the session is first created (\u001b[94m_sessions.putIfAbsent\u001b[m). That works well with the current auto-titling flow\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K (since auto-titling runs before the first message creates the session), but if thread renaming is ever added\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K later, the existing session's system instructions will ret"]
[0.000, "o", "ain the initial title.\u001b[K\r\n  3. \u001b[1mComposer State Shared Across Thread Switches\u001b[m\n\u001b[44D\u001b[1K • \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jke574019f330a822e;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/markdown_composer.dart#L27-L30\u0007MarkdownComposer\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 holds a single \u001b[94mTextEditingController\u001b[m not keyed by \u001b[94mactiveThreadId\u001b[m. If a user types a draft in\r\n\u001b[5C\u001b[1K Thread A and clicks Thread B in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk8015991529845862;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/thread_sidebar.dart\u0007ThreadSidebar\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, the unsent draft remains in the input box for Thread B.\r\n\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[60C\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[34;1m> 1. Add a concept of projects that set a working directory for the Antigravity harness.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  2. I'm guessing workspaceOnly enables commands that are inside the sandbox. We should add UI that allows programs to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  be run that want to escape the sandbox, but only after review by the user.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  3. Update README.md and add `/skills/` to `.gitignore`.\u001b[m\u001b[K"]
