[0.000, "o", "projects that set a working directory for the Antigravity harness.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  2. I'm guessing workspaceOnly enables commands that are inside the sandbox. We should add UI that allows programs to\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  be run that want to escape the sandbox, but only after review by the user.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1m  3. Update README.md and add `/skills/` to `.gitignore`.\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 3m 7s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(Initial analysis suggests that the `workspaceOnly` setting within the observed package might c...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 5 files \u001b[37m(policy.dart, hooks.dart, capabilities.dart, +2)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m \u001b[37m(grep -rn \"workspaceOnly\\|enableSandbox\\|confirmRunCommand\\|disable_sandbox\\|DisableSandbox\\|sandbox\" /Users/...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[37m… 12 more actions (9 reads, 3 commands) …\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mExplored\u001b[m 1 file \u001b[37m(README.md)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m 7 commands \u001b[37m(+2 · strings ~/.antigravi... ×3 · python3 -c ' with op... ×2)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n  I am inspecting"]
[0.000, "o", " the \u001b[94mlocalharness\u001b[m binary's sandbox and policy handling and will follow up as soon as the check\r\n  finishes.\r\n\n\u001b[37m○\u001b[m \u001b[37mThought for 1m 9s\u001b[m \u001b[37m(The `package:antigravity` configuration relies on `workspaces` to define the working directory...)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[32m●\u001b[m \u001b[33;1mRan\u001b[m 3 commands \u001b[37m(python3 -c ' with op... ×3)\u001b[m \u001b[37m(ctrl+o to expand)\u001b[m\r\n\n\u001b[33;1m?\u001b[m How should projects and conversation threads be organized in the UI?\r\n\u001b[34;1m> (Recommended) Projects group threads (project switcher + New Project dialog with a working directory path, filtering\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[34;1mthreads by active project)\u001b[m\r\n⡿  \u001b[94mWor\u001b[90mking...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: In /diff, press c to add inline comments and send them as feedback.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m▸ Please fix issues highlighted in the review (alt+m to send immediately)\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
