[0.050, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\r\u001b[29A  Right now \u001b]8;id=jk93fed6b4ac309b3;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L103\u001b\\\u001b[4;34;4mC\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mh\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ma\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mR\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4me\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mp\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mo\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ms\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mi\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mo\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mr\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4my\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m.\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4md\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4me\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mf\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ma\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mu\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ml\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mA\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4m2\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mu\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mi\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mC\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ma\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mt\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ma\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4ml\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mo\u001b[m\u001b[4;34;4mg\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u001b\\ uses the stock \u001b[94mbasicCatalog()\u001b[m. Because \u001b[94ma2ui_flutter\u001b[m's\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[?5W\u001b[J  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2d13076c940c00cd;file:///Users/brett/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/a2ui_flutter-0.1.0/lib/src/component_implementation.dart#L50\u0007ComponentImplementation\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 lets you pair any JSON Schema with a Flutter widget builder, we can extend the catalog with\r\n  developer-focused components tailored to an Antigravity coding assistant:\r\n\n  • \u001b[94mCodeDiffC"]
[0.000, "o", "ard\u001b[m: Renders a side-by-side or unified diff preview with \u001b[1mApply Patch\u001b[m / \u001b[1mDiscard\u001b[m action buttons that\r\n  trigger an \u001b[94mActionMessage\u001b[m back to the Antigravity agent.\r\n  • \u001b[94mFileTreeCard\u001b[39;1m / \u001b[94;22mWorkspaceFileCard\u001b[m: Renders clickable file badges (\u001b[94mpath\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlineStart\u001b[m, \u001b[94mlineEnd\u001b[m, \u001b[94msummary\u001b[m) for files in\r\n  the active \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd07341abd224fee0;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/domain/models/chat_models.dart#L21\u0007ChatProject.workingDirectory\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\r\n  • \u001b[94mCommandRunnerCard\u001b[m: Lets the agent propose a shell command with editable flags/arguments (\u001b[94mTextField\u001b[m / \u001b[94mCheckBox\u001b[m\r\n  bound to the surface data model) and a \u001b[1mRun in Workspace\u001b[m button.\r\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### Option 3: Persistent Split-Pane \"Surface Canvas\" Drawer (Alongside Inline Chat Surfaces)\u001b[m\r\n\n  As noted in \u001b[94ma2ui_agent\u001b[m's \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2aa98b8fadb77e0;file:///Users/brett/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/a2ui_agent-0.1.0/lib/src/utils/renderer_state.d"]
[0.000, "o", "art#L59-L65\u0007RendererState\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, A2UI supports two UX modes over the same \u001b[94mMessageProcessor\u001b[m: \u001b[1minline chat\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[1mturns\u001b[m and a \u001b[1mpersistent canvas\u001b[m where multi-turn prompts iteratively evolve a single surface.\r\n\n  • \u001b[1mWhat we can build\u001b[m:\n\u001b[16D• Add a toggleable right-hand \u001b[1mA2UI Inspector / Canvas pane\u001b[m in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd4d5118fab63289a;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/chat_screen.dart#L70-L136\u0007ChatScreen\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkb68a85abea9e7a9c;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/top_toolbar.dart\u0007TopToolbar\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007.\n\u001b[88D• Pin any active surface from \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk325cd969d2af6056;file:///Users/brett/.pub-cache/hosted/pub.dev/a2ui_core-0.5.0/lib/src/core/surface_group_model.dart#L107\u0007renderer.model.allSurfaces\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 into the side canvas, with a live \u001b[1mData Model JSON\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[6C\u001b[1minspector\u001b[m (\u001b[94msurface.dataModel\u001b[m) and \u001b[1mComponent Tree viewer\u001b[m so you can watch data bindings (\u001b[94m@"]
[0.000, "o", "path\u001b[m) and component\r\n\u001b[6Cupdates mutate in real time as you chat.\r\n\n  ──────\r\n  \u001b[1m### Option 4: Self-Healing Validation Loop (Automatic LLM Repair on \u001b[94mAnswerErrorPart\u001b[39m)\u001b[m\r\n\n  Currently, if the LLM emits a malformed \u001b[94m<a2ui-json>\u001b[m block or violates a component schema,\r\n  [\u001b[94mStreamedAnswer\u001b[m](file:///Users/br\r\n⣽  \u001b[94mGener\u001b[90mating...\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m└ Tip: In request-review mode, file edits are shown for approval before being applied.\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[94m>\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[90m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
