[0.016, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[29A\u001b[1m### 2.3. Renaming a Thread Destroys Its Active Agent Session History\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  In \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkd12eeb00afdac37a;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/view_models/chat_view_model.dart#L515-L531\u0007ChatViewModel.renameThread\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 and \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk2b210417ea75be83;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L509-L525\u0007ChatRepository.getOrCreateSession\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007:\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[94m_sessionMetadata\u001b[m includes \u001b[94mthreadTitle\u001b[m. Whenever a thread is renamed, \u001b[94mcloseThreadSession(threadId)\u001b[m is called (and\r\n  \u001b[94mexistingMeta == desiredMeta\u001b[m becomes \u001b[94mfalse\u001b[m), which calls \u001b[94mexistingSession.stop()\u001b[m.\u001b[K\r\n  • Stopping the \u001b[94mAgent\u001b[m session terminates the \u001b[94mlocalharness\u001b[m conversation context for that thread, so the next message\r\n  in that thread starts a brand-new agent session with no memory of prior messages in the thread.\u001b[K\r\n  • Additionally, in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkcb9af0cc82436321;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy"]
[0.000, "o", "_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/view_models/chat_view_model.dart#L658\u0007ChatViewModel.sendMessage\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007, \u001b[94mfinal shouldAutoTitle = !current.isAutoTitled || current.messages.\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94misEmpty;\u001b[m will overwrite a user-supplied title if the user renamed an empty thread before sending their first\u001b[K\r\n  message (also note that \u001b[94mrenameThread\u001b[m currently has no UI trigger in \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk4d0da6dd58b49721;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/thread_sidebar.dart\u0007ThreadSidebar\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 or \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jkf34777d5a7054b40;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/ui/features/chat/views/widgets/top_toolbar.dart\u0007TopToolbar\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007).\u001b[K\r\n  ──────\u001b[K\r\n  \u001b[1m## 3. Security & Sandbox Heuristics\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[1m### 3.1. Command Path Parsing False Positives & Bypass Vectors\u001b[m\r\n\u001b[K\n  \u001b[34;4m\u001b]8;id=jk4460770e458f9c81;file:///Users/brett/tmp/agy_genui_demo/lib/data/repositories/chat_repository.dart#L293-L331\u0007ChatRepository.findOutsideWorkspacePathInCommand\u001b[m\u001b]8;;\u0007 "]
[0.000, "o", "tokenizes \u001b[94mcommandLine\u001b[m via \u001b[94mRegExp(r'''[\\s\"'\u001b[m;|&><()]+''')` and\r\n  checks prefixes:\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\n  • \u001b[1mFalse Positives\u001b[m: Non-path arguments starting with \u001b[94m/\u001b[m after quote stripping—such as \u001b[94mawk '/pattern/' file.txt\u001b[m or \u001b[94msed\u001b[m\r\n  \u001b[94m's/foo/bar/'\u001b[m—are treated as absolute paths (\u001b[94m/pattern/\u001b[m) outside the workspace and trigger sandbox-escape prompts.\u001b[K\r\n  • \u001b[1mFalse Negatives\u001b[m:\u001b[K\r\n      • Flags with \u001b[94m=\u001b[m assignments such as \u001b[94mcurl --output=/etc/foo\u001b[m or \u001b[94mgit --git-dir=/tmp/repo status\u001b[m start with \u001b[94m--\u001b[m,\r\n\u001b[6Cbypassing the \u001b[94mtoken.startsWith('/')\u001b[m check.\u001b[K\n\u001b[42D• Environmen`\u001b[K\n\n\n\n\n\u001b[17D\u001b[?2026l"]
